Z||000018||Carrolles||01-06-2000||04:31 PM||||At the nationals in St. Louis I talked to a guy who had installed a GT-40 kit on his Fiero.  The kit cost $6995 and included everything but paint.  It looked very nice.  No cutting etc either.||||reg||1
Z||000019||mshill||01-06-2000||04:57 PM||||Phil, I am really not to new to the subject of building up a car.  In 1978 I rebuilt a 1970 Trumph GT6 from the ground up including a complete swap of the body from the firewall back with new upholstery and paint.  If I do a Lambo, I will get it with the subframe complete and body mounted just to avoid the cutting and welding part of it.  I am painfully aware of the cost of building a kit, but in April I get a $20K bonus from work so I am going to have some fun.<P>Carrolles, I am familiar with the GT-40 as well and that is an option, but my wife and kids are set on a real eye popper, so the Lambo or F50 are all that really stand out at this time.||||reg||1
